<META NAME="Description" CONTENT="The American Housing Survey (AHS) collects data on the Natinal's housing, including apartments, single-family homes, mobile homes, vacant housing units, household characteristics, income, housing and neighborhood quality, housing costs, and recent movers.  National data are collected every other year, and data for each of 46 selected Metropolitan Areas are collected about every four years, with an average of 12 Metropolitan Areas included each year.  The survey is conducted by the Bureau of the Census for the Department of Housing and Urban Development.">

<META NAME="Keywords" CONTENT="American Housing Survey, housing, housing units, house, houses, home, homes, homeownership, homeowner, home owner, mobile homes, units in structure, new construction, stories in structure, housing unit size, home value, value, purchase price, mortgage, owners, renters, housing characteristics, housing characteristics by age, housing characteristics by sex, year built, housing costs, housing quality, housing condition, neighborhood, fuels, utilities, household composition, substandard housing, appliances">

</HEAD>

